(a) All license holders under this chapter must provide, in writing, an individual to be designated the contact person who is a county resident for all licenses issued pursuant to this chapter as follows:
(1) If the license holder is a county resident, then said license holder shall be the contact person;
(2) If the license holder is not a county resident, the license holder must designate one employee officer, property owner or lessor of the location, or an attorney who is a county resident as the contact person;
(3) The license holder must, in writing, designate the contact person on the forms provided by the city upon initial application, renewals and/or changes in the contact person;
(4) A contact person is subject to all provisions of this chapter;
(5) If the contact person ceases to meet the requirements of a contact person, then the license holder must, within three business days, notify the city, and a new contact person must be employed, named and appointed by the license holder within ten business days from the previous contact person's termination as such;
(6) All service of notices and/or violations required by this chapter may be made to the contact person in lieu of the license holder for the purposes of this chapter. The license holder shall be responsible for any service of any notice to the contact person and for any and all actions;
(7) If at any time an establishment licensed under this chapter does not have a contact person except as provided for in this section, then said establishment cannot sell alcoholic beverages, and must immediately cease the sale of all alcoholic beverages and post a notice on the premises on all doors open to the public, until a new contact person has been designated;
(8) If a licensee operates an establishment without a contact person, except as provided for in subsection (2) of this section, then said licensee is subject to the suspension and revocation of his license as provided for in this chapter for all violations of this chapter;
(9) A contact person under this chapter must meet all requirements and qualifications for which he serves and must meet the additional qualifications provided, which shall be required during the entire period that the licensee shall hold the license.
(b) The contact person must be a resident of the county.
(Ord. No. 2020-012, § 1, 9-28-2020)

